// Bellmourn after the green star: what its people say now that a man in black smallclothes has come
// down in a comet on one of Lord Velscour's Sworn and climbed out of the crater. They take him for
// Tessariel, the Sacred Flame of their holy texts (the Canticle of Embers, the Litany of the Ninth
// Bell, the Book of the Green Star, Saint Ivo's Testament), sent to kill the Demon Lord Velscour; and
// they whisper it, because Velscour's sycophants kill anyone who speaks the name. Same shapes as
// townscripts.js: a line is [speaker, text], speaker 0 or 1 of the pair; {a} and {b} are what speaker
// 0 and speaker 1 are called. Every chat line fits a two- or three-line bubble.
//
// A conversation's tags say who may hold it: 'any' (anyone), 'gossip' (any two grown-ups, now and
// then), or a calling (guard, worker, merchant, smith, baker, healer, hunter, gentry, traveller, old,
// young, farmer, innkeeper, learned, priest, couple, velscour: Lord Velscour's garrison). A calling tag
// means speaker 0 holds that calling; 'couple' is only for husband and wife.

